# PROJECT: BELT PANIC!
## Build a Colourful Third-Person Multiplayer Party Game

Act as a senior 3D game developer, multiplayer engineer, gameplay designer, and UI/UX designer.

Your task is to build a fully playable, colourful, cartoonish 3D multiplayer party game called **BELT PANIC!**

The game should have the fun, chaotic atmosphere of Stumble Guys and Fall Guys, with original characters, original environments, and its own unique gameplay mechanics.

IMPORTANT: This is NOT a horror game.

The game should be bright, funny, colourful, goofy, and competitive.

---

# 1. GAME CONCEPT

All players spawn together inside one enclosed arena room.

In the exact centre of the room, there is a pedestal containing one special belt.

Players rush towards the belt.

Whoever picks up the belt becomes the HUNTER.

The Hunter must chase and tag the other players using the belt.

However, there is a twist:

The room lights constantly switch ON and OFF.

- When lights are ON, the Hunter hunts everyone.
- When lights are OFF, survivors get an opportunity to hunt the Hunter and steal the belt.

The player who steals the belt becomes the next Hunter when the lights turn back ON.

This creates a continuous cycle of hunting, hiding, escaping, and stealing.

The entire game should feel chaotic and unpredictable.

# 2. CAMERA AND PLAYER PERSPECTIVE

THIS IS A STRICT REQUIREMENT.

Use a THIRD-PERSON CAMERA.

Absolutely NO top-down camera.
Absolutely NO first-person camera.
Absolutely NO isometric camera.

The camera must stay behind and slightly above the player's character, similar to third-person party games.

Camera requirements:

- Smooth third-person follow camera.
- Mouse-controlled camera rotation.
- Character visible at all times during normal gameplay.
- Smooth camera movement.
- Camera collision detection.
- Camera should not pass through walls or objects.
- Sensible camera distance.
- Character should face the movement direction.
- Smooth character rotation.
- Slight camera smoothing when changing directions.

The player should feel like they are directly controlling a little 3D character.

